  "question": {
    "text": "From the base of a pole of height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math>&nbsp;meter, the angle of elevation of the top of a tower is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. The pole subtends an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> at the top of the tower. Then the height of the tower is:",
    "image": null
  },
